Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of large filesystem sizes exceeding 8 TB (2^31 * 4096 bytes) in the `netsnmp_fsys_calculate32` function. The original implementation did not properly adjust the values of `units_32`, `avail_32`, and `used_32` when the size exceeded the 32-bit integer limit, leading to potential overflow and incorrect calculations. The patch corrects this by shifting the values appropriately based on the size, ensuring that they remain within the bounds of 32-bit integers.
